# GitHub Integration

## Connection

GitHub CLI (`gh`) is pre-authenticated. Use it for all GitHub operations.

### Common commands

```bash
# PR overview
gh pr view <number> --repo merchantos/<repo> --json title,state,isDraft,baseRefName,additions,deletions,changedFiles,body,author,labels

# CI status
gh pr checks <number> --repo merchantos/<repo>

# List PR files (use this when gh pr diff hits the 300-file limit)
gh api repos/merchantos/<repo>/pulls/<number>/files --paginate \
  | jq -r '.[] | "\(.status) \(.additions)+/\(.deletions)- \(.filename)"'

# Full diff
gh pr diff <number> --repo merchantos/<repo>

# Read file at a specific ref (handy when the PR branch isn't fetched locally)
gh api "repos/merchantos/<repo>/contents/<path>?ref=<branch_or_sha>" --jq '.content' | base64 -d

# Review history
gh api repos/merchantos/<repo>/pulls/<number>/reviews
gh api repos/merchantos/<repo>/pulls/<number>/comments
gh api repos/merchantos/<repo>/issues/<number>/comments

# Thread resolution state (REST doesn't expose it)
gh api graphql -f query='
query {
  repository(owner: "merchantos", name: "<repo>") {
    pullRequest(number: <number>) {
      reviewThreads(first: 50) {
        nodes { isResolved isOutdated path line }
      }
    }
  }
}'

# Get full 40-char head SHA (required for posting inline comments)
gh api repos/merchantos/<repo>/pulls/<number> --jq '.head.sha'
```

## Posting an inline comment (when explicitly requested)

Use a JSON file via `--input` to avoid shell escaping issues with multi-line bodies and code suggestions:

```bash
cat > /tmp/comment.json <<'EOF'
{
  "body": "...",
  "commit_id": "<full-40-char-sha>",
  "path": "<file>",
  "line": <n>,
  "side": "RIGHT"
}
EOF

gh api --method POST "repos/merchantos/<repo>/pulls/<number>/comments" --input /tmp/comment.json
```

`commit_id` MUST be the full 40-character SHA — abbreviated SHAs return `422 commit_id is not part of the pull request`.

The line must be inside a changed hunk; a non-hunk line yields `pull_request_review_thread.line` errors.
